<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico assigns all six secondary auctions.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico assigns all six secondary auctions.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico has completed all six credit auctions whereby it sought to drain liquidity of 5.409 billion pesos in the secondary market on Thursday, dealers said.</p>
<p>CREDIT AUCTIONS   TERM     MAX    MIN     AVERAGE BIDS BIDDERS</p>
<p>  1.100    bln pesos  15 days  25.90  25.75   25.84   5    4</p>
<p>  1.100    bln pesos  13 days  26.00  25.84   25.92   8    6</p>
<p>  900  million pesos   8 days  25.60  25.50   25.56   7    4</p>
<p>  800  million pesos   7 days  25.50  24.45   25.48   3    3</p>
<p>  755  million pesos   4 days  25.11  25.10   25.10   1    1</p>
<p>  754  million pesos   1 day   24.77  24.75   24.76   3    3</p>
<p>NOTE - The maximum, minimum and average are percentages.</p>
<p>((--Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9500))</p>
